# Phase 12, first slice: the Pane window server runs as a user program on a
# shared mapping of /dev/fb0 and the input devices, a client puts a window
# on the screen through the port protocol with a shared-memory buffer, and a
# 10x10 damage recomposites only those 100 pixels. The kernel desktop hands
# the screen over for the test and takes it back afterwards.
cerberus kernel shell
!send pane --test
!wait 30
pane: screen
pane: client connected
pane: window 1 created
pane: full commit composited
pane: content verified
pane: 10x10 damage recomposited 100 px
pane: PASS
run: /bin/pane exited with status 0
!send gui
!wait 2
gui:
